        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "Explain why you cannot prove $3+8+13+\\cdots+(5n-2)=\\dfrac{n(5n+1)}{2}$ for all real numbers using mathematical induction.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Induction covers successive integer values of $n$, not all real numbers.",
          "worked": "Starting from an integer base case, the step from $k$ to $k+1$ reaches successive integers only. It does not cover all real numbers. Also, $n$ counts the terms in this finite sum and must be a positive integer.",
